# Extended regular expression, case-insensitive, matched against
# tools/cocoapods-compat/README.md by tools/validate/validate.sh.
#
# D11 (resolved 2026-08-02) settled that CocoaPods is not supported and deliberately
# recorded no activation condition, because a condition written on the page reads as a
# route a consumer can ask for. This file lists the formulations that would reopen it.
# It is data, not prose: everything after the comment block is one single-line ERE.
#
# tools/validate/probe-d11-guardrail.sh proves the pattern against sentences that must
# match and against the real wording of the README, which must not. Change the pattern
# and the probe together, never one alone.
awaiting (human )?confirmation|proposal awaiting|private specs repository|git-tag podspec|separate approval|(may|can|could|will|would|shall) be (enabled|activated|supported|published)|(will|would|shall) (publish|enable|activate|support)|(enabled|activated|supported|published) (only )?(after|once|upon|if)|supported paths?( are| is)|opt in
